  "cut_point": "We are given:\n\n- For any positive integer $ n \\geq 10 $, define $ N_n = \\{1, 2, 3, \\cdots, n\\} $.\n- Let $ A \\subseteq N_n $, and $ |A| \\geq 10 $.\n- We are to find the **maximum value of $ n $** such that for **every** subset $ A \\subseteq N_n $ with $ |A| \\geq 10 $, the **maximum difference** between any two distinct elements in $ A $ is **at most 10**, i.e.,\n  $$\n  \\max_{\\substack{a, b \\in A \\\\ a \\neq b}} |a - b| \\leq 10\n  $$",
